+- **Dirty pushed file.** A file whose introducing commit was on `origin/master`, then locally rewritten, was still `SAFE(pushed)`. Removal still requires a clean path.
+- **Self-referential ledger.** Verify returned `SAFE(moved-to-obsidian)` when source and vault were the same file. Vault returned `NOT-VERIFIED(source-equals-vault)`.
+- **Symlink digest.** A directory digest that contains a symlink is not `moved-to-obsidian`.
+- **Hidden-only stale reference.** Citation only in a dotfile → tool `SAFE(stale)`. Require `--hidden` before acting.
+- **Invented scratch types.** `*.tmp`, `out/`, and "older than the lane's last admitted round" are not the tool rule. An old `*.tmp` was `NOT-SAFE(none)`.
+- **Unpushed named-branch worktree.** `git worktree list` saying `prunable` is not a receipt. `wt-r98` was `NOT-SAFE(unpushed-branch)` with `dir=absent`.
